//#line 1 "track.cone"
// Tracks: one animated value as a pure function of time. A Track holds keys
// (a time, a value, and how to get from this key to the next) and answers
// 'eval(t)' for any t, with no state, so it can be scrubbed, seeked and run
// backwards. Before the first key it holds the first value, after the last it
// holds the last (a Clip decides looping).
//
// - TYPED VALUES. A key's value is a few floats, laid out by the track's kind:
//   f32 (1), Vec2 (2), Vec3 (3), Quat (4, x y z w as glTF has it), Color (4,
//   linear RGBA, mixed in a named space), bool and discrete (1 each, always
//   step), transform (10: translation 3, rotation 4, scale 3), and a vector
//   of any length (for morph-target weights). Quaternions are blended by
//   spherical interpolation along the shortest arc and are always unit length;
//   a spline over quaternions is run on the four numbers and normalised, the
//   way glTF specifies.
// - INTERPOLATION PER KEY, for the segment from that key to the next:
//   step; linear (with an optional easing id: a Penner curve, smoothstep or a
//   spring); bezier (CSS cubic-bezier handles on the segment's progress);
//   catmull (a Catmull-Rom spline through the neighbouring keys, tangents by
//   central difference over the actual key times, one-sided at the ends);
//   hermite (tangents given per key: 'inTan' arrives, 'outTan' leaves, in
//   value per second). glTF's CUBICSPLINE is exactly this Hermite form, so
//   INTERP_CUBICSPLINE is the same id.
// - CATMULL-ROM here is the non-uniform finite-difference form (Kochanek and
//   Bartels with zero tension, bias and continuity), not the centripetal
//   variant: it is C1, it passes through every key, and linear data stays
//   linear.

pub const TK_F32 = 0u32;
pub const TK_VEC2 = 1u32;
pub const TK_VEC3 = 2u32;
pub const TK_QUAT = 3u32;
pub const TK_COLOR = 4u32;
pub const TK_BOOL = 5u32;
pub const TK_DISCRETE = 6u32;
pub const TK_TRANSFORM = 7u32;
pub const TK_VECN = 8u32;

pub const INTERP_STEP = 0u32;
pub const INTERP_LINEAR = 1u32;
pub const INTERP_BEZIER = 2u32;
pub const INTERP_CATMULL = 3u32;
pub const INTERP_HERMITE = 4u32;
pub const INTERP_CUBICSPLINE = 4u32;

